      "id": "jiv30ib",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Constitutional Articles Related to Prime Minister and Council of Ministers"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Prime Minister is appointed by the President under Article 75 of the Constitution.",
        "The Council of Ministers is collectively responsible to the Lok Sabha as specified under Article 75(3).",
        "The Prime Minister serves as the principal channel of communication between the President and the Council of Ministers under Article 78.",
        "A non-member of Parliament can be appointed as a Minister or Prime Minister, but must get elected to either House within 6 months.",
        "The Council of Ministers comprises three tiers: Cabinet Ministers, Ministers of State, and Deputy Ministers."
      ],
      "id": "0j0hyfb"
    },
